::PC_U02_L05_Q_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U02_L05_Q_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.3
Question:
Which reasoning best supports verifying the identity sin^2(x)+cos^2(x)=1 in a solution? Use item context 1 to select the best answer.
{
~A. Substitute one angle only and assume the identity is always true #This choice uses a related idea but does not complete the required reasoning for the stated standard.
~B. Move terms randomly until both sides look similar #This choice reflects a common misconception or an incomplete step.
~C. Divide by sine even when sine may equal zero #This choice does not match the conditions in the question.
=D. Use the Pythagorean identity and show that the left side simplifies to the right side #Correct. This answer follows the lesson concept and connects the result to the stated standard.
}

